How I measured: with my own read-only harness, /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-ren-theories/4cd2c9b9-8aca-4fd1-99bb-ff1a3f9d1698/scratchpad/trim/verify/mine.py. It splices the proposed four points under the unchanged comment and time line, renders them with the real navigation.first_screen, the records and the opening, then applies measure_layers.part(README, None, '^## ') and count(). The current README measures 172. The proposal measures 165: title 4, nav 14, banner 18, time line 5, then 22/44/24/34, rendering '1–2 minutes'. The rendered page is at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-ren-theories/4cd2c9b9-8aca-4fd1-99bb-ff1a3f9d1698/scratchpad/trim/verify/README.proposed.md. The trimmer's floor re-measures at 154.

Kept, and checked:
- the leading comment and the time line, byte for byte;
- all six fields, as written;
- the eight links, with the same targets;
- both premises, with their content and roles ('fixes scope, whose losses count'; 'alone gives order');
- 'unasserted' and 'their warrant open';
- the ethics nowhere said to derive from the condition;
- no person or AI named;
- all four points, the last ending 'No human review yet.';
- 'evaluation included', 'comes to be' and the glossary's gloss of the condition;
- the receipt sentence (FS1 and FS2), verbatim;
- 'tests frozen before scoring' (FS8's accepted fix), verbatim;
- a failure stated;
- 'a first-person conviction';
- the banner, unchanged and consistent with Ren's 'not the finalized version' (sources/15-codex-theory-conversations/2026-10-31-push-a-working-version.md);
- the one page and the overview, which indeed state no times at their tops.

Point 4's change can be adopted as it stands. 'Passed and failed tests frozen before scoring' keeps the failure and the frozen tests, and removes the partitive misreading. It no longer matches ONE-PAGE's 'some passed and some failed', which FS3's refutation cited, but nothing on the never-cut list depends on that.

Suggested fix for point 2: '**Its ethics**, [argued as life's way](…#theses) (thesis T8), rests on [two unasserted premises](…), their warrant open, with no warrant binding every possible mind claimed: …'. This uses 07's own construction and AGENTS's phrase, and brings back the glossary's standing and the identifier. Point 2 becomes 48 words and the screen 169, measured; the file is /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-ren-theories/4cd2c9b9-8aca-4fd1-99bb-ff1a3f9d1698/scratchpad/trim/verify/points-fix.md.

Either the comment or the landing's study section should then name the reading times and 'evaluation included' as part of the excess. The comment is not shown on the page, so changing it does not touch the no-names rule. No repository file was edited and no git command was run.
